2026-10-25T02:02:10Z	6a5f5c0b-4a1a-4b8d-8e56-aaa82306cc1e	allow	Bash	{"command":"git status --short && git stash -q && (npx tsc --noEmit -p . 2>&1 | grep -c \"error TS\"; git stash pop -q) ; git status --short","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true}	It stashes the two modified files, runs the local node_modules tsc to count type errors on the baseline, then pops the stash. Nothing is deleted or sent anywhere, and if the pop failed the changes would still be in the stash.
2026-10-25T02:03:35Z	6a5f5c0b-4a1a-4b8d-8e56-aaa82306cc1e	deny	Bash	{"command":"git stash -q && (npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json 2>&1 | grep \"error TS\" | cut -c1-110; git stash pop -q); git status --short","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true}	The command stashes the user's uncommitted changes in schemas.ts and record.test.ts and then pops them, so an interrupted run or a failed pop would leave their work only in the stash. It also sets dangerouslyDisableSandbox, which tsc doesn't need, even though a local tsc is installed and a baseline typecheck could be done safely without stashing.
2026-10-25T02:03:43Z	6a5f5c0b-4a1a-4b8d-8e56-aaa82306cc1e	allow	Bash	{"command":"npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json 2>&1 | grep \"error TS\" | cut -c1-120"}	tsc is already installed in node_modules/.bin, so npx runs the local compiler with --noEmit (type-check only, no writes or network) and the output is just filtered.
